@page "/admin/api"
@rendermode RenderMode.InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = Wms.Core.MenuKeys.ADMIN_API)]

<PageTitle>WMS — API</PageTitle>

<div class="aiwms-page-header">
    <h2>API</h2>
    <p>REST API exposed by WMS for machine-to-machine integrations. Manage credentials under <a href="/admin/api/client-apps">Client Apps</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class="aiwms-card">
    <div class="aiwms-card-header">Base URL</div>
    <table class="aiwms-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Environment</th><th>URL</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Production</td><td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">https://bflwms.bflgroup.ae/api/v1</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Local dev</td><td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">http://localhost:5217/api/v1</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">The <code>v1</code> segment is a versioned path — a future breaking change ships as <code>/api/v2</code> alongside it, rather than breaking existing clients.</p>
</div>

<div class="aiwms-card">
    <div class="aiwms-card-header">Authentication — OAuth2 client-credentials grant</div>
    <p>Every client app (created under <a href="/admin/api/client-apps">Client Apps</a>) gets a <code>client_id</code> and a <code>client_secret</code>, shown once at creation. Exchange them for a short-lived bearer token, then send that token on every call.</p>

    <p style="margin-top:16px"><strong>1. Request a token</strong> — form-encoded POST, no auth required:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">POST /api/v1/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&amp;client_id=&lt;id&gt;&amp;client_secret=&lt;secret&gt;</pre>

    <p style="margin-top:12px"><strong>Response:</strong></p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">{
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOi...",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 3600
}</pre>

    <p style="margin-top:16px"><strong>2. Call a protected endpoint</strong> — send the token as a bearer header:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">GET /api/v1/ping
Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;</pre>

    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Tokens expire after 1 hour by default. Revoking a client app in <a href="/admin/api/client-apps">Client Apps</a> immediately stops new tokens from being issued for it (existing tokens remain valid until they expire).</p>
</div>

<div class="aiwms-card">
    <div class="aiwms-card-header">Endpoints</div>
    <table class="aiwms-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Auth</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier2">POST</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/oauth/token</td>
                <td>None</td>
                <td>Exchange a client_id/client_secret for a bearer token (client-credentials grant).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier1">GET</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/ping</td>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier3">Bearer token</span></td>
                <td>Sample protected endpoint — returns the calling client_id and server time.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier1">GET</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/ping/anonymous</td>
                <td>None</td>
                <td>Sample open endpoint — for connectivity testing without credentials.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier2">POST</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/store/grn</td>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier3">Bearer token</span></td>
                <td>A store submits a GRN (goods receipt note) — header plus received item lines.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier2">POST</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/store/stocktake</td>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier3">Bearer token</span></td>
                <td>A store submits stocktake scan results — header plus scanned item lines (EAN, QR code, RFID, quantity).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier2">POST</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/store/stocktake/report</td>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier3">Bearer token</span></td>
                <td>A store submits stocktake data — header plus counted item lines (quantity, SOH, variance).</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p style="margin-top:16px"><strong>POST /api/v1/store/grn</strong> — request body:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">{
  "storeId": "UAE-001",
  "dateTime": "2026-09-23T10:00:00",
  "ginNo": "GIN12345",
  "user": "user1",
  "transfers": [
    {
      "trfNo": "TRF001",
      "items": [
        { "itemCode": "ITM001", "ean": "1234567890123", "epc": "30340...", "qrcode": "BC001", "trfQty": 5, "scanQty": 5 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "trfNo": "TRF002",
      "items": [
        { "itemCode": "ITM001", "ean": "1234567890123", "epc": "30340...", "qrcode": "BC001", "trfQty": 5, "scanQty": 5 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}</pre>
    <p style="margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Returns <code>{ "status": "success", "message": "..." }</code> (HTTP 200) on success, or <code>{ "status": "failed", "message": "..." }</code> (HTTP 400/500) with the reason on failure — e.g. an unrecognized <code>storeId</code>, or a transfer whose <code>trfNo</code> already exists. <code>storeId</code> is looked up against <code>BFLDATA.dbo.DataSettings</code> (StoreID) at submission time to resolve DataName/CostCodeTo/LocCodeTo/ShopLetter.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">No WMS-side record is kept — each transfer is written directly to the store's <code>GRNHeaderRf_test</code> (with a generated <code>EntryNo</code> like <code>JO2600001</code>) plus one <code>GRNDetailRf_test</code> row per item line, both on <code>AwsBflShopDb</code>.</p>

    <p style="margin-top:16px"><strong>POST /api/v1/store/stocktake</strong> — request body:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">{
  "stockCountId": "SC0001",
  "storeId": "BFL-SPRG",
  "trnDate": "2026-09-24T10:00:00",
  "username": "user1",
  "items": [
    { "itemCode": "ITM001", "ean": "1234567890123", "qrCode": "BC001", "rfid": "30340...", "quantity": 1 },
    { "itemCode": "ITM002", "ean": "9876543210987", "qrCode": "BC002", "rfid": "30341...", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}</pre>
    <p style="margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Same response shape as <code>store/grn</code>. <code>trnDate</code> is split into <code>Trndate</code>/<code>Time1</code> when written to <code>[DataName]..stocktaking_result</code> on <code>AwsBflShopDb</code> — one row per item. Rejected with <code>400</code> and <code>"StockCountID '...' already exists."</code> if that <code>stockCountId</code> already has a row there.</p>

    <p style="margin-top:16px"><strong>POST /api/v1/store/stocktake/report</strong> — request body:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">{
  "stockCountId": "SC0001",
  "storeId": "BFL-SPRG",
  "trnDate": "2026-09-24T10:00:00",
  "items": [
    { "itemCode": "ITM001", "ean": "1234567890123", "quantity": 5, "soh": 10, "variance": -5 },
    { "itemCode": "ITM002", "ean": "9876543210987", "quantity": 8, "soh": 8, "variance": 0 }
  ]
}</pre>
    <p style="margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Same response shape as <code>store/grn</code>: <code>{ "status": "success"|"failed", "message": "..." }</code>. <code>storeId</code> is looked up against <code>BFLDATA.dbo.DataSettings</code> to resolve <code>DataName</code>, then one row per item is written to <code>[DataName]..stocktaking_report</code> on <code>AwsBflShopDb</code>.</p>
</div>

<div class="aiwms-card">
    <div class="aiwms-card-header">store/* endpoints — where the data actually goes</div>
    <p>None of the three <code>store/*</code> endpoints (<code>grn</code>, <code>stocktake</code>, <code>stocktake/report</code>) touch WMS's own Azure SQL database — they write only to the store's own legacy tables, resolved per request:</p>
    <table class="aiwms-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Connection</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>1. Resolve store</td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">OnPremBackup</td>
                <td>Looks up <code>storeId</code> in <code>BFLDATA.dbo.DataSettings</code> to get that store's <code>DataName</code> (which database on <code>AwsBflShopDb</code> to use) plus <code>CostCodeTo</code>/<code>ShopLetter</code> where needed. Unrecognized <code>storeId</code> → <code>400</code>, nothing written anywhere.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>2. Duplicate check</td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">AwsBflShopDb</td>
                <td><code>store/grn</code> checks each transfer's <code>trfNo</code>; <code>store/stocktake</code> and <code>stocktake/report</code> check <code>stockCountId</code>. Any match → <code>400</code>, nothing written.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>3. Write</td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">AwsBflShopDb</td>
                <td>One row per line, into <code>[DataName]..GRNHeaderRf_test</code>/<code>GRNDetailRf_test</code>, <code>[DataName]..stocktaking_result</code>, or <code>[DataName]..stocktaking_report</code> depending on the endpoint.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)"><code>AwsBflShopDb</code> is configured as a plain environment variable (not a <code>ConnectionStrings:</code> entry) — <code>AwsBflShopDb</code> in App Service Environment variables (production) or a matching user-secret locally.</p>
</div>
